* 012-6921:L4:1 same-terminal-polarity hypothesis
RL4_1 h_outputbase l4_internal_1 {horizontal_compensation_r}
LL4_1 l4_internal_1 h_outbase {horizontal_compensation_l}
* 012-6921:L4:2 same-terminal-polarity hypothesis
RL4_2 h_outputbase l4_internal_2 {horizontal_compensation_r}
LL4_2 l4_internal_2 h_outbase {horizontal_compensation_l}
* 012-6921:L4:3 same-terminal-polarity hypothesis
RL4_3 h_outbase l4_internal_3 {horizontal_compensation_r}
LL4_3 l4_internal_3 h_outbase {horizontal_compensation_l}
* Bounded engineering families, NOT measured SC237E/SF1260/SF1280 curves.
.model HOR_D D(IS=1n N=1.5 RS=2 CJO=2p TT=5n)
.model HOR_N NPN(IS=1e-14 BF=100 VAF=80 CJE=20p CJC=8p TF=2n TR=10n)
.model HOR_DRIVER_N NPN(IS=1e-12 BF=60 VAF=80 CJE=150p CJC=80p TF=20n TR=100n)
.subckt HORIZONTAL_TRIM top wiper bottom
Ra top wiper {1000*(1-horizontal_trim_fraction)}
Rb wiper bottom {1000*horizontal_trim_fraction}
.ends HORIZONTAL_TRIM
* Tapped, phase-inverting tank. Inductance is PER HALF winding.
.subckt HORIZONTAL_TANK left middle right
Ra left a {horizontal_tank_r}
Rb right b {horizontal_tank_r}
La a middle {horizontal_tank_l}
Lb middle b {horizontal_tank_l}
Kcore La Lb {horizontal_coupling}
.ends HORIZONTAL_TANK
* Opposite polarity secondary for turn-off transformer drive.
.subckt HORIZONTAL_DRIVER top collector base ground
Rp top p {horizontal_driver_r}
Lp p collector {horizontal_driver_l}
Rs s base {horizontal_secondary_r}
Ls ground s {horizontal_driver_l/horizontal_driver_ratio^2}
Kcore Lp Ls {horizontal_coupling}
.ends HORIZONTAL_DRIVER
* Output families and normal-operation ancillary components; no SOA claim.
.model HOR_Z6 D(IS=1n N=1.5 RS=2 BV=6.2 IBV=1m)
.model HOR_RECT D(IS=10n N=1.5 RS=.2 CJO=20p TT=100n)
.model HOR_HV_RECT D(IS=1n N=2 RS=100 CJO=1p TT=100n)
.model HOR_OUTPUT_N NPN(IS=1e-10 BF=20 VAF=100 CJE=1n CJC=200p TF=100n TR=500n)
.subckt HORIZONTAL_CHOKE a b
Rloss a n {horizontal_choke_r}
Lcore n b {horizontal_choke_l}
.ends HORIZONTAL_CHOKE
.subckt HORIZONTAL_LINEARITY a b
Rloss a n {horizontal_linearity_r}
Lcore n b {horizontal_linearity_l}
.ends HORIZONTAL_LINEARITY
.subckt HORIZONTAL_COMPENSATION a b
Rloss a n {horizontal_compensation_r}
Lcore n b {horizontal_compensation_l}
.ends HORIZONTAL_COMPENSATION
.subckt HORIZONTAL_BRIGHTNESS low wiper high
Ra low wiper {1meg*horizontal_brightness_fraction}
Rb wiper high {1meg*(1-horizontal_brightness_fraction)}
.ends HORIZONTAL_BRIGHTNESS
.subckt HORIZONTAL_FOCUS high wiper low
Ra high wiper {1meg*(1-horizontal_focus_fraction)}
Rb wiper low {1meg*horizontal_focus_fraction}
.ends HORIZONTAL_FOCUS

* Generic devices; historical connectivity does not establish device accuracy.
.model VERTICAL_NPN_BOUND NPN(IS=1e-14 BF={vertical_bf} VAF=60 CJE=20p CJC=8p TF=2n TR=20n)
.model VERTICAL_DIODE D(IS=2n RS=2 N=1.7 CJO=2p TT=5n)
.model VERTICAL_PNP_BOUND PNP(IS=1e-14 BF={retrace_bf} VAF=60 CJE=30p CJC=10p TF=5n TR=50n)
* LM723-family functional equivalent: TI SNVS765C p2 metal-can pin contract.
* cs inv noninv ref vminus out collector vplus compensation current-limit
* NOT a transistor-level Tesla MAA723 model. No thermal/SOA qualification.
* Assumed gm 1 mS, gain 10000, +/-200 uA drive and 30 pF internal pole.
.subckt MAA723_BOUND cs inv noninv ref vm out vc vp comp cl
Breference ref_i vm V={min(7.15,max(v(vp,vm)-2.35,0))}
Rreference ref_i ref 10
Breference_draw vp vm I={max(i(Breference)*-1,0)}
Bquiescent vp vm I={1.7m*min(max(v(vp,vm)/9.5,0),1)}
Rinput inv noninv 10Meg
Bdrive_up vp comp I={max(min(.001*v(noninv,inv),200u),0)*min(max(v(vp,vm)/9.5,0),1)}
Bdrive_down comp vm I={max(min(-.001*v(noninv,inv),200u),0)*min(max(v(vp,vm)/9.5,0),1)}
Rgain comp vm 10Meg
Cinternal comp vm 30p
Dupper comp vp M723_CLAMP
Dlower vm comp M723_CLAMP
Qpass vc comp out M723_PASS
Qlimit comp cl cs M723_LIMIT
Rout out vm 1Meg
.model M723_PASS NPN(IS=1e-14 BF=100 VAF=60 CJE=30p CJC=10p TF=5n)
.model M723_LIMIT NPN(IS=1e-14 BF=100 VAF=60)
.model M723_CLAMP D(IS=1e-12 RS=10)
.ends MAA723_BOUND

* Provisional P09A substitute: LM709 manufacturer internal circuit.
* TI/National SNOS659A, PDF page 4 (printed 3), metal-can pin order.
* Port order: compensation A, inverting, noninverting, V-, output
* compensation, output, V+, compensation B. Board DIP pins: 3,4,5,6,9,10,11,12.
* Resistors/topology transcribed; transistor parameters are engineering
* assumptions, NOT characterized P09A/LM709 silicon. No SOA/thermal model.
.subckt LM709_FAMILY ca inv noninv vm co out vp cb
Q1 n1 noninv tail N709
Q2 ca inv tail N709
Q3 n3 n1 e3 N709
Q4 n3 e3 bias N709
Q5 cb ca e5 N709
Q6 cb e5 bias N709
Q7 vp n3 e7 N709
Q8 vp cb e8 N709
Q9 co bias n9e P709
Q10 tailbase tailbase vm N709
Q11 tail tailbase tail_e N709
Q12 c12 co e12 N709
Q13 vm c12 out P709
Q14 vp c12 out N709
Q15 bias_top bias_top bias N709
R1 e7 n1 25k
R2 e7 ca 25k
R3 e3 bias_top 3k
R4 e5 bias_top 3k
R5 vp n3 10k
R6 vp cb 10k
R7 e8 n9e 1k
R8 bias tap 3.6k
R9 n9e tap 10k
R10 tap tailbase 10k
R11 tail_e vm 2.4k
R12 co e12 10k
R13 e12 vm 75
R14 vp c12 20k
R15 n9e out 30k
.model N709 NPN(IS=1e-14 BF=100 VAF=100 CJE=4p CJC=2p TF=.2n TR=20n)
.model P709 PNP(IS=1e-14 BF=50 VAF=50 CJE=4p CJC=2p TF=20n TR=100n)
.ends LM709_FAMILY

* Engineering bounds, not fitted factory transistor curves.
.model VERT_Z16 D(IS=1n N=1.5 RS=2 BV=16 IBV=1m)
.model VERT_POWER_N NPN(IS=1e-12 BF={output_bf} VAF=80 CJE=200p CJC=80p TF=20n TR=200n)
.model VERT_POWER_P PNP(IS=1e-12 BF={output_bf} VAF=80 CJE=200p CJC=80p TF=20n TR=200n)
* Source R58 remains one inventoried device; no duplicate source identities.
.subckt VERT_POT top wiper bottom
Ra top wiper {470*symmetry_fraction}
Rb wiper bottom {470*(1-symmetry_fraction)}
.ends VERT_POT

* Generic bounded models; not specimen-calibrated SF1260/ZC5.1.
.model REG5_NPN NPN(IS=1e-14 BF={reg5_bf} VAF=60 CJE=40p CJC=15p TF=20n TR=100n)
.model REG5_ZENER D(IS=1n RS=5 N=1.5 BV=5.1 IBV=.005 CJO=100p)
.subckt REG5_POT top wiper bottom
Rtop top wiper {100*reg5_position}
Rbottom wiper bottom {100*(1-reg5_position)}
.ends REG5_POT

* BOUNDED GENERIC FAMILY MODELS: not manufacturer-calibrated SSY20A/1AD50.
* Every free parameter and its exploratory bounds is declared in the profile.
.model SSY20A_BOUND NPN(IS={q_is} BF={q_bf} VAF={q_vaf}
+ TF={q_tf} TR={q_tr} CJE={q_cje} CJC={q_cjc})
.model 1AD50_BOUND D(IS={d_is} N={d_n} RS={d_rs} CJO={d_cjo} TT={d_tt})

* Bounded functional models, NOT fitted 74S37/T200 device curves.
* Source E03 NAND logic is evaluated by the digital adapter upstream.
.subckt S37_DRIVER logic output ground params: resistance=1 slew=1
Btarget target ground V={driver_low+(driver_high-driver_low)*v(logic,ground)}
Redge target edge 1k
Cedge edge ground {driver_tau*slew/1000}
Boutput output ground I={(v(output,ground)-v(edge,ground))/(resistance*(driver_r_low+(driver_r_high-driver_r_low)*min(1,max(0,(v(edge,ground)-driver_low)/(driver_high-driver_low)))))}
.ends S37_DRIVER
* Input current is an explicit assumed TTL loading law; no implied logic input
* at 0.5 VCC. Threshold and transition span have independent bounded parameters.
.subckt GATE a b y ground supply
Ba a ground I={20u-220u/(1+exp((v(a,ground)-gate_threshold)/gate_span))}
Bb b ground I={20u-220u/(1+exp((v(b,ground)-gate_threshold)/gate_span))}
Ca a ground {gate_input_c}
Cb b ground {gate_input_c}
Btruth truth ground V={1-1/(1+exp(-(v(a,ground)-gate_threshold)/gate_span))/(1+exp(-(v(b,ground)-gate_threshold)/gate_span))}
Rdelay truth smooth 1k
Cdelay smooth ground {gate_tau/1000}
Boutput y ground I={(v(y,ground)-(.15+max(v(supply,ground)-.95,0)*v(smooth,ground)))/(10+70*v(smooth,ground))}
.ends GATE
.subckt T200_BOUND a1 b1 y1 a2 b2 y2 ground y3 a3 b3 y4 a4 b4 supply
Xg1 a1 b1 y1 ground supply GATE
Xg2 a2 b2 y2 ground supply GATE
Xg3 a3 b3 y3 ground supply GATE
Xg4 a4 b4 y4 ground supply GATE
.ends T200_BOUND
.model Z9_BOUND D(IS=1n N=1.5 RS=5 BV=9.1 IBV=1m CJO=30p)

